course: dictionary
lesson: 11058
title: The weekend
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A weekend is the two days at the end of the week: Saturday and Sunday. «Ruby-Lou has two homes: Mum's flat on school days and Dad's house at weekends.» Here weekends means the days when school is closed, so Ruby-Lou stays at Dad's house on Saturday and Sunday.
explain: People say it in different ways. In the UK they say «at the weekend», and in the USA and Australia they say «on the weekend». Both mean the same thing, so the word itself stays the same.
explain: In maths, a week has 7 days: 5 weekdays and 2 weekend days. If a question asks how many weekend days there are in one week, the answer is 2.
fact: A weekend is Saturday and Sunday.
fact: A weekend can also be a short holiday or trip over those two days, called a «weekend away».
fact: «Over the weekend» means during Saturday and Sunday.
fact: A long weekend has a holiday on Monday or Friday, so there is an extra day off.
fact: Weekdays are Monday to Friday, and a week has 5 of them.
exercise: «Ruby-Lou has two homes: Mum's flat on school days and Dad's house at weekends.» On which days does Ruby-Lou stay at Dad's house? | *Saturday and Sunday | Only on public holidays | Monday and Tuesday | Wednesday to Friday
exercise: How many weekend days are there in one week? | 7 | 1 | *2 | 5
exercise: Which phrase is used in the UK for the weekend? | on the weekend | last weekday | *at the weekend | over the week
test: What is a weekend? | A kind of school lesson | The first day of the month | Monday to Friday | *Saturday and Sunday, the days at the end of the week
test: Which phrase means the weekend that has just passed? | every weekday | *last weekend | next weekend | a weekday holiday
exam: What makes a weekend long? | Two extra weeks of school | Going to bed late every night | A trip on a Wednesday | *A holiday on a Monday or Friday
